WEBVTT

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.110
Kurahara?

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.970
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.340
<b>Shirakaba Loop</b>

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:56.510
Are you satisfied running 
with the friends you finally made?

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:59.420
Are you satisfied holding hands and
running around with your little friends?!

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:06.780
Kakeru!

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.380
See? You haven't changed.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:35.880
You're always ruining someone else's efforts.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.340
You don't see your teammates!

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.090
Kakeru.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.300
I don't know if you're just naturally talented,

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:46.470
but if you think you alone will
manage somehow, you're wrong!

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.480
Kakeru.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:51.770
Kakeru.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:55.930
Kakeru!

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.490
Don't forget that we're here.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.770
What did he do?

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:16.130
Hey, what are you doing?

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:18.330
Get your stuff on the bus!

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.380
Yes, sir!

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:30.990
We'll show you just how serious
we are at the qualifier.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.420
Oh, right.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:39.860
You first-years will be too busy
with chores to watch the race.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.840
Start by becoming regulars on your team.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:44.910
Good luck.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:57.340
<b><i>And Then Start Running</i></b>

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.310
Your time hasn't even improved by ten seconds!

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.570
What kind of training have you been doing?

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:14.400
Sorry!

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:16.810
Aren't you a scholarship student?

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:20.200
Your only option is to do well at running.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.110
Go run ten more kilometers!

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.030
Yes, sir!

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.840
The same goes for the rest of you.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.160
Results are everything for runners.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.380
I won't allow any weakness!

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:39.820
Yes, sir!

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.910
Kurahara.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:03.150
Hey, Kurahara.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:08.130
These men are prefectural officials.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:09.770
You won with a huge lead.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.770
Thank you.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:14.720
You must be a top runner nationally, as well.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:17.320
You can really see the results
of your coaching.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:20.510
I'm just blessed with talented runners.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.600
We're looking forward to this year's
prefectural and national races.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.550
I hope we can meet your expectations.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:31.680
Apparently, they want me to speak
at a party about fostering athletes.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.070
I've asked the coaches to manage
your training schedule, so don't worry.

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:35.980
Yes, sir.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.310
It's all thanks to what you've achieved.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:43.040
Hey, you! Don't walk so slowly!

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.190
Look sharp!

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:46.900
Don't damage Sendai Josei High School's dignity!

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.890
We'll be doing high-altitude training.

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:55.490
We'll be able to enjoy the scenery.

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:59.530
Seems gentle. Right?

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:00.330
What?

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:04.340
The ground seems like 
it'll be gentle on our knees.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:18.850
Your leg hurts?

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:24.270
Can't you come up with a better excuse?

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:29.860
Everyone has an injury or two
they're working through.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:33.180
Runners improve their times despite them. Run!

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:34.030
Yes, sir!

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:37.730
I'll be cutting everyone who doesn't do well.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.260
Prepare yourselves!

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:41.660
He doesn't get it.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:43.670
It can't be helped. He's a first-year.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:48.810
Tell him he only needs
to try when he's watching.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.200
You tell him.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.310
He won't listen to me.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:54.520
After all, he's a scholarship student.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:05.140
If you can't do it,

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:09.610
I don't think you have to run.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:20.650
Have you ever suffered an injury?

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:23.850
Didn't think so.

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:36.510
Hey!

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:38.030
Hey.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.350
It's Hana.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.210
Hey!

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:49.670
I see meat.

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:52.400
Those bags are full of meat.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.370
I'll cook dinner tonight!

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.930
No, wait!

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:02.330
Wait, wait!

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:05.620
You're on bathroom duty tonight.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:06.980
Use your head.

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:11.030
Quit surrounding Hana, you sweaty pigs!

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.450
What's wrong?

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:20.110
Isn't it a little soon for you to be tired?

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.700
Yes!

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:30.030
There's plenty more!

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:33.740
My special crunchy liver and leek
stir fry contains tons of vegetables!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.700
Thanks for the meal!

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:39.450
That's it. They're making me feel great.

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:45.660
Do you want to quit the team?

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:48.550
Look at all of you.

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:53.490
If you can't be useful here,
you won't be useful anywhere.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:56.490
Your life will be decided here.

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:59.340
Do you understand that? Do you?

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:00.060
Yes, sir!

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.980
I don't know how fast you were in the boonies,

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.520
but here we coach based on years of theory.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:12.030
If you can't keep up, it's because
you're not good enough.

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:13.360
Yes, sir.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.890
I can't hear you!

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:17.130
You don't get it, do you?

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:18.060
Yes, sir!

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:22.560
Listen up. Imagine you're racing for your life!

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:23.330
Yes, sir!

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:26.420
Don't forget that you're representing
a prestigious school!

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:27.450
Yes, sir!

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.120
Leave behind those who can't run!

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:30.500
We don't have time for them!

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:31.490
Yes, sir!

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.340
<b></b>

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:41.820
You can't handle it?

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:45.740
This year... This time,
I don't think I'll be able to.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:46.810
But by next year—

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:50.150
You can't close the gap that quickly.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:55.580
Everyone's pouring their blood,
sweat, and tears into practice

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:58.150
every day while you're resting.

00:09:58.150 --> 00:09:59.240
Don't worry.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.160
The team will manage without you.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:09.560
Get yourself healed up and find a new path.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:19.520
Please! I'm here on a track scholarship!

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:23.280
If I quit the team, I won't have anything!

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:25.770
Please let me run! Please!

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:26.990
Please!

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.150
Please! Please!

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:34.200
It's time. Let's get started.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.380
Yes, sir. To the track!

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:37.740
Yes, sir!

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.410
Please! Please let me back on the team!

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:46.140
I'm sorry I got injured! Please!

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:47.740
Please!

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:57.760
I only have time for students who can run.

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:03.430
Good luck. You have my support.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:39.970
Kurahara?

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.060
Kakeru.

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:46.720
Kakeru.

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:47.630
Kakeru?

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:52.570
Um...

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:56.470
He asked you to lead Group B since
we're splitting into two groups.

00:11:56.470 --> 00:11:58.380
Quit spacing out.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:11:59.750
Sorry.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:31.450
You must be cold.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.850
I heated up some milk.

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:37.860
Look at those stars.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:41.110
It'd be a waste not to see this.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:51.580
How much do you know?

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.400
About me.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:55.710
How much?

00:12:56.280 --> 00:13:00.810
You knew the morning
after I first stayed at Aotake

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:05.400
that I was from Sendai Josei High School.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.140
Yeah.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.990
Which means...

00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:14.100
A quick search online revealed
just how good a runner you were.

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:17.600
That you were a nationally top-ranked
runner by your second year,

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:21.390
and that your records suddenly
stopped the spring of your third year.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:25.320
But that's all I know.

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:28.690
There was no need for me 
to investigate any further.

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:35.100
I can't cause the team any more trouble
than I have already.

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:41.080
I can't control my emotions.

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:46.740
When that reporter spoke to me, 
I felt like I had woken up from a dream.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:51.390
I realized no matter
how far I run, I'm still me.

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:53.920
Haiji, I—

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:54.790
Kakeru.

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:58.730
If you're going to talk, why not tell everyone?

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:01.730
It's okay.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:04.670
No matter what happens, we're still us.

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:09.790
You're still awake.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:12.360
Sorry you had to bathe last.

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:13.760
Was the bath dirty?

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:14.960
Not at all.

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:16.940
You cleaned it again for me, didn't you?

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:18.520
Well, yeah.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:20.750
Really? You're that considerate?

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.720
Yuki told me to use my head.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:26.890
Your seniors can teach you
all kinds of things.

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:28.680
By the way...

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:31.540
Kakeru, do you have a girlfriend?

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:32.420
What?

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:35.100
Seriously? I wanna know!

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:39.310
O-Of course I don't. Where did that come from?

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:44.140
Well, the night sky was just so pretty.

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:46.930
What does that mean?

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:47.720
What?

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:49.700
The stars are mad pretty!

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.370
Right?

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:51.070
Yeah!

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:52.260
You'll wake the others!

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:53.540
Look, Hana. A shooting star.

00:15:03.850 --> 00:15:05.240
Dad?

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:14.330
I hated my high school track team.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:20.060
My coach's methods,
the stuffy air of that club room...

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:22.600
I hated it so much, it made me want to puke.

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:28.180
I broke my coach's nose,
lost my college recommendation,

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:29.540
and quit the club.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:35.730
Since the school wanted to keep it quiet,
they imposed restrictions on the team.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:38.060
The summer of my third year,

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:45.520
none of my classmates 
were able to participate in meets.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.270
Looking back on it,

00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:53.370
what happened to that first-year
was just an opportunity for me

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:59.460
to release all my pent-up anger
and achieve some self-satisfaction.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:04.220
It's no wonder they hate me.

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:11.110
Because of a moment's decision,
I wasted three years of their effort.

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.280
Especially for Sakaki...

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.280
I see.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:17.920
That's why he hates you so much.

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:20.860
It's no wonder he hates me.

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:26.920
I became unable to see anything but myself.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.350
That's what I'm afraid of.

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:32.170
I'm worried I might do something similar again.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:37.780
I was nearly unable to stop myself again.

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:46.060
You've been hesitant about running
because you were worried about that?

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:49.790
But you had a reason, right?

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:52.150
A reason you had to do it.

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:56.030
It's not good to use violence
against another person, though.

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:58.450
Yes. That's why...

00:16:58.450 --> 00:16:59.530
That's why?

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:03.750
That's why...

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:10.430
Before I cause any more trouble for you guys...

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:13.700
Before that, I...

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:14.670
Hey.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:19.320
We've already started running.

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:22.350
We won't let you bail on us now.

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:24.810
They're right.

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:27.270
If anything, I'm glad to know.

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:29.510
Thanks for telling us.

00:17:29.510 --> 00:17:34.780
We more or less already knew that
you tend to act before you speak.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:38.210
If anything, I can't believe
you were worried about that.

00:17:38.210 --> 00:17:39.240
Yeah.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:45.170
Kakeru, I really like you.

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:46.660
Don't the rest of you?

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:47.690
Yeah.

00:17:50.050 --> 00:17:53.050
It's hard to say yes when
you're asked face-to-face.

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.490
When we first met,

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:02.430
I was captivated by the way you ran.

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.230
I was moved.

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:08.370
I couldn't believe someone 
could have such pure running form.

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:13.470
I thought you might already
know the answer I was seeking.

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:18.490
What it means to run.
The answer to that question.

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:23.710
But I still haven't found the answer.

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:28.210
The more I run, the more
difficult I realize it is.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:30.930
Don't you feel the same way?

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:34.890
I have fun running with you!

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:38.340
Me, too. In fact, I have more fun than Jota!

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.610
You what?

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:41.050
I was just speaking my mind.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:44.220
Don't ruin the moment!

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.540
Yeah, but...

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:46.810
Me, too.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:51.750
I enjoy running with you guys,
from the bottom of my heart.

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:58.900
Kakeru, the goal is still far ahead.

00:18:59.350 --> 00:19:01.870
Let's go there together.

00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:21.950
Hey!

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:26.560
Breakfast is getting cold!

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:29.070
We'll be right there!

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:32.120
All right, that concludes our meeting.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:36.940
Sorry.

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:38.670
For what?

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:41.650
You don't need to apologize.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:46.610
Thank you for believing in me.

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:50.660
You're welcome.

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:54.490
I want to run.

00:19:56.070 --> 00:19:59.440
In the Hakone Ekiden with this team!

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:05.640
Let's aim for the top together.

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.640
Let's run it together.

00:20:09.010 --> 00:20:10.580
The Hakone Ekiden.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:13.860
I'm serious!

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:15.770
Starting now, I'm serious about it!

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:20.510
Huh?

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:23.250
I can't help it.

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:27.430
Hey, guys. Kakeru's finally
ready to take things seriously.

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:30.520
He said he's serious about
running at Hakone starting now.

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:32.520
What? Seriously?

00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:34.760
I thought we already were.

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:37.250
Then what have we been doing until now?

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:38.740
No, I—

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:50.340
Let's go, Kakeru.

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:52.690
Yeah.

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:42.670
Next time: “You're Not Alone.”

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:45.990
<b>Next time: You're Not Alone</b>
